**How to implement.** The refractiveindex.info adapter over an offline snapshot of its GitHub database (001 §D '1. refractiveindex.info (CC0): an offline snapshot of the GitHub database plus "Update snapshot". The existing YAML importer (`MaterialImport`) is REUSED as the record parser'; the S13.1 brief: HTTP goes through one marked seam and no test calls it, and tests use fixture snapshots under the test output; .spec-md §4 'Errors and IO', 'Stored formats', 'Every kit and catalogue write is atomic'). The snapshot is the archive's `database/catalog-nk.yml` and `database/data/**`, held under `<materialSourcesFolder>/refractiveindex.info/` beside its stamp `.snapshot-json` (001 §A: a file that exists once per folder is named by its extension alone). The archive is read through S6's archive seam, the app's one zip reader (`KitArchiveProxy.create ()`, step 199: `listZipEntries` reads every name through `KitTreeEntry.tryOfZipEntryName`, so no entry escapes, and `extractKitZip` reports and reads the cancellation per file and removes what it wrote), so no second extractor is written. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.1. (1) The stamp's schema: new `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/material-source-snapshot.schema.json`, draft 2020-12 with `$id` `https://berreman/schema/material-source-snapshot.json`, in the shape of `schema/kit-history.schema.json` (step 167): `schemaVersion` a positive integer, checked unconditionally; only under `if` it is 1 (`then`), exactly the keys `schemaVersion`, `source` and `sourceVersion`, both non-empty strings. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside `schema/kit-history.schema.json`'s in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no comment. `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `validateSourceSnapshot (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` over `validateWith` (step 29), its schema loaded once behind a `lazy`, as `validateKitHistory` is. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialSourceStore.fs`, `module MaterialSourceStore` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `KitArchiveStore.fs` (step 199): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. It opens `System.IO`, `System.Net.Http`, `System.Threading`, `OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit`, `OpticalConstructor.Domain.KitArchive`, `OpticalConstructor.Domain.LibraryEntryFiles`, `OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialSources` and `MaterialImport`. In order: (a) `SourceSnapshotStamp = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; source : MaterialSourceName; sourceVersion : MaterialSourceVersion }` with `static member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` (1), `extension : FileExtension` (`.snapshot-json`, the one place that text is written) and `fileName : FileName` (`(FileStem.ofText "").withExtension SourceSnapshotStamp.extension`), the shape of `KitFile` (step 122). `SourceSnapshotText of string` with `.value` is the stamp file's text, as `KitHistoryText` is the history file's (step 167): `member this.fileText : Result<SourceSnapshotText, StorageError>` on the stamp is `nodeOf this` rendered by `canonicalFileText` (steps 27, 124), and `member this.parseStamp : Result<SourceSnapshotStamp, StorageError>` on the text is `parseVersionedText validateSourceSnapshot SourceSnapshotStamp.extension SourceSnapshotStamp.currentSchemaVersion this.value` (step 124): no up-converter and no fallback reader. (b) `SourceArchiveUrl of string` with `.value`, and `[<ReferenceEquality>] SourceArchiveDownloader = { downloadArchive : SourceArchiveUrl -> FileName -> CancellationToken -> Result<unit, MaterialSourceError> }`, which writes the archive at the URL into the file. `static member http : SourceArchiveDownloader` is the ONE HTTP seam of the online sources and carries `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof IoBoundary, "the one HTTP seam of the online material sources (001 §D): a GET streamed into a file; every exception is SourceDownloadErr")>]`: an `HttpClient` made and disposed per call sends a GET with `HttpCompletionOption.ResponseHeadersRead` and the token, requires a success status, and copies the body into a `FileStream` in `FileMode.Create`; every exception is `SourceDownloadErr` naming the URL and the message. No test calls it: tests pass a downloader that copies a zip they wrote. (c) `type MaterialSourceProxy with static member createRefractiveIndexInfo (sources : FolderName) (downloader : SourceArchiveDownloader) (clock : ClockProvider) : MaterialSourceProxy`, unique on its receiver beside `createInMemory` (ELEV019). Building it touches nothing. `sourceName` is `MaterialSourceName "refractiveindex.info"`, the snapshot folder `<sources>/refractiveindex.info`, the licence `EntryLicence "CC0-1.0"` (the database's README: CC0 1.0 Universal) and the archive `SourceArchiveUrl "https://github.com/polyanskiy/refractiveindex.info-database/archive/refs/heads/main.zip"`, each written there alone. Every file is read as bytes and decoded as UTF-8 with a leading byte-order mark dropped, as a kit's files are (step 126). `snapshotVersion ()`: no stamp file answers `Ok None`; otherwise the parsed stamp's `sourceVersion`, an `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` being `UnsupportedSnapshotSchemaErr` and any other `StorageError` `SourceSnapshotIoErr`, each with its `describe`. `searchRecords query`: without a stamp `SourceSnapshotMissingErr`; otherwise `query.filter` (step 443) of `RefractiveIndexInfoCatalogText.hits` (step 445) over `database/catalog-nk.yml`, an import error being `SourceSnapshotIoErr` with its `describe`. `fetchRecord record`: without a stamp `SourceSnapshotMissingErr`; a record the catalog's hits do not list, or whose text `KitRelativePath.tryCreate` (step 123) refuses, `SourceRecordMissingErr` naming it; otherwise the bytes of `database/data/<record>` give `recordHash = ContentHash.ofBytes <the bytes>` (step 123) and their text `importMaterial` (an error being `SourceRecordUnreadableErr` naming the record and the error's `describe`), and the answer is `{ pull = { source; record; recordHash; sourceVersion = <the stamp's>; licence; citation }; material = { <the import> with name = <the hit's name> } }`, the citation being `EntryCitation "refractiveindex.info, <record>"` followed, when `referencesOpt` (step 445) answers one, by `: ` and its text. `updateSnapshot observer`, in this order, every name below lying beside the snapshot folder in `sources`: any `refractiveindex.info.zip.tmp`, `refractiveindex.info.tmp` or `refractiveindex.info.old` an interrupted run left is deleted; the archive is downloaded into `refractiveindex.info.zip.tmp` with `observer.cancellation`; a cancelled token then answers `SourceSnapshotCancelled`, whatever the download answered, and a download error is answered as it is. `KitArchiveProxy.create ()`'s `listZipEntries` of the zip (a `KitArchiveError` being `SourceArchiveInvalidErr` with its `describe`) gives the entries; the archive's one top-level folder `<top>` MUST hold the file `<top>/database/catalog-nk.yml`, else `SourceArchiveInvalidErr`; the entries kept are that file and every file and folder under `<top>/database/data/`. `extractKitZip { zip = <the zip>; entries = <those>; target = KitFolder (FolderName <refractiveindex.info.tmp>) }` runs under a `KitArchiveObserver` that tells `observer.reportSnapshotProgress` each `KitArchiveProgress` as a `SourceSnapshotProgress` of the same counts and whose cancellation is `observer.cancellation`: `KitArchiveCancelled` answers `SourceSnapshotCancelled`. On `KitArchiveFinished n` the stamp `{ schemaVersion = currentSchemaVersion; source = sourceName; sourceVersion = MaterialSourceVersion <clock.now ()'s UTC date as yyyy-MM-dd, invariant culture> }` is written into `refractiveindex.info.tmp/<top>` through `FileName.writeBytesAtomically` (step 126); a held snapshot folder is moved to `refractiveindex.info.old`, `refractiveindex.info.tmp/<top>` is moved to the snapshot folder, and the `.old` folder, the `.tmp` folder and the zip are deleted, so the snapshot is replaced whole; the answer is `SourceSnapshotUpdated { version; files = SourceSnapshotFileCount n }`. Every exception, and every error after the download, deletes what this run made, moves `.old` back when it was moved, and keeps the held snapshot; an exception is `SourceSnapshotIoErr` naming the folder and the message. A declaration whose signature carries a bare primitive for this IO is marked on itself with `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof IoBoundary, …)>]`, as step 199's are. No package is added (`System.Net.Http` ships with .NET), and no retry, cache, mirror, second URL or setting is added (.spec-md §8). (3) The `MaterialSourceProxy` doc (step 443) names `createRefractiveIndexInfo` beside the in-memory double in one line. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialSourceFixture.fs`, `module MaterialSourceFixture`, and `OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialSourceStoreTests.fs`, `module MaterialSourceStoreTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended in that order at the end of the compile list with no comment. The fixture, each member with a one-line doc: `siPage ()` and `glassPage ()` are the texts of `fixtures/Si.yml` and `fixtures/formula2.yml`; `changedSiPage ()` is `siPage ()` with `0.700 3.785 0.013` replaced by `0.700 3.790 0.013`; `freshSources (owner : string) : FolderName` is a new GUID-named folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, owner)`, never under `%TEMP%`; `writeSnapshot (snapshot : string) (si : string) : unit` writes, under `snapshot`, `fixtures/catalog-nk.yml` (step 445) as `database/catalog-nk.yml`, `si` as `database/data/main/Si/nk/Test.yml`, `glassPage ()` as `database/data/glass/test/BK7/nk/Test.yml` and the stamp of `2026-11-01` through `SourceSnapshotStamp.fileText`; `writeArchive (zip : string) (si : string) : unit` writes, through `ZipArchive`, a GitHub-style archive whose one top folder `refractiveindex.info-database-main/` holds `README.md`, `database/tools/x.py`, the folder entries of `database/data/` and below, and the three files `writeSnapshot` writes but the stamp; `copyingDownloader (zip : string) (asked : ResizeArray<SourceArchiveUrl>) : SourceArchiveDownloader` records each URL and copies `zip` into the target file; and `fixedClock (instant : DateTime) : ClockProvider` answers that UTC instant. Facts, each over a fresh sources folder whose snapshot is `<it>/refractiveindex.info`: `a refractiveindex.info source without a snapshot answers no version and refuses search and fetch`: `snapshotVersion` is `Ok None`, and `searchRecords` and `fetchRecord` are `SourceSnapshotMissingErr`. `a snapshot's catalog is searched with the shared rule`: over `writeSnapshot` of `siPage ()`, `snapshotVersion` is `2026-11-01`, `silicon` finds `main/Si/nk/Test.yml` alone, and a blank query finds both pages in catalog order. `a fetched page is MaterialImport's material under its hit's name, with the page's hash, the stamp's version, CC0 and its citation`: the Si record's `material.physics` equals that of `(RefractiveIndexInfoText (siPage ())).importMaterial`, its name is `Si (Silicon), Test 2026: n,k 0.25–0.70 µm`, its `recordHash` is `ContentHash.ofBytes` of the page file's bytes, and its pull holds `refractiveindex.info`, `2026-11-01`, `CC0-1.0` and the citation `refractiveindex.info, main/Si/nk/Test.yml: <the page's REFERENCES text>`; the glass record's physics equals `formula2.yml`'s import; and a record the catalog does not list, and `../x.yml`, answer `SourceRecordMissingErr`. `an update downloads the archive and replaces the snapshot with its catalog and data, file by file`: over a held snapshot, `updateSnapshot` with `copyingDownloader` of `writeArchive` of `changedSiPage ()` and `fixedClock` of 2026-11-04 answers `SourceSnapshotUpdated` of `2026-11-04` and three files, its progress reading 1 to 3 of 3; the one URL asked is the database's archive; the snapshot holds exactly `.snapshot-json`, `database/catalog-nk.yml` and the two pages, with no `README.md` or `tools`; the Si page's hash is the changed page's; and `sources` holds nothing else, no `.tmp`, `.old` or zip. `an update cancelled before its next file keeps the held snapshot`: a token whose source is cancelled on the first progress answers `SourceSnapshotCancelled`; the snapshot still holds `2026-11-01` and its files byte for byte, and `sources` holds nothing else. `an archive without the database catalog is refused and the held snapshot kept`: an archive holding `README.md` alone answers `SourceArchiveInvalidErr`, and the snapshot is unchanged. `a failed download keeps the held snapshot`: a downloader answering `SourceDownloadErr "offline"` answers it, and the snapshot is unchanged. `a snapshot stamp of another schema version is refused`: a stamp whose `schemaVersion` is 2 makes `snapshotVersion` answer `UnsupportedSnapshotSchemaErr`.

**Acceptance.** After the adapter lands, a test MUST instantiate the real `MaterialSourceProxy.createRefractiveIndexInfo` over a fixture snapshot under the test output, its fetch MUST parse a page through `MaterialImport` under the page's hash, the stamp's version, CC0 and its citation, and its update MUST replace the snapshot whole through the archive seam or keep it; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a refractiveindex.info source without a snapshot answers no version and refuses search and fetch`, `a snapshot's catalog is searched with the shared rule`, `a fetched page is MaterialImport's material under its hit's name, with the page's hash, the stamp's version, CC0 and its citation`, `an update downloads the archive and replaces the snapshot with its catalog and data, file by file`, `an update cancelled before its next file keeps the held snapshot`, `an archive without the database catalog is refused and the held snapshot kept`, `a failed download keeps the held snapshot` and `a snapshot stamp of another schema version is refused`, the count rising by 8; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s43 invariants MUST pass.
